@startuml
title CAVR — Dependency Assurance Sequence
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
actor Developer
participant "CAVR Service" as CAVR
participant "Artifact Resolver" as RES
participant "Contract / Policy" as POLICY
participant "Capability & Threat Checks" as CHECK
participant "Advisory Source" as ADV
participant "Scanner / Fixture" as SCAN
participant "Verdict Cache" as CACHE
database "Evidence Store" as STORE
Developer -> CAVR : assess candidate dependencies
CAVR -> RES : resolve supported manifests and lock data
RES --> CAVR : exact package artifacts + hashes
CAVR -> POLICY : evaluate package allowlist and policy
POLICY --> CAVR : permitted / rejected / unresolved
loop each resolved package
  CAVR -> CHECK : evaluate contract, capabilities, threats
  CHECK --> CAVR : package signals
  CAVR -> ADV : query enabled advisory source
  ADV --> CAVR : advisory result / unavailable
  CAVR -> CHECK : inspect source triggers and rule coverage
  CHECK --> CAVR : static findings and coverage gaps
  CAVR -> CACHE : lookup by artifact, lock, contract, policy, advisory, rules
  alt eligible clean VERIFIED result
    CACHE --> CAVR : cached evidence
  else cache miss or prior non-clean outcome
    CACHE --> CAVR : no reusable clean result
    opt supported high-risk trigger on Python artifact
      CAVR -> SCAN : run counterfactual fixture for supported Python artifact
      SCAN --> CAVR : findings / inconclusive
    end
    CAVR -> STORE : persist package evidence; cache VERIFIED only
  end
end
CAVR -> CAVR : aggregate per-package status
note right of CAVR
Per package precedence:
REJECTED > UNRESOLVED > VERIFIED
end note
CAVR --> Developer : result + evidence provenance
@enduml
